  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nIs a ₱200,000 donation to a friend subject to donor's tax under the TRAIN law?\n\n### Short Answer\nYes, a ₱200,000 donation to a friend is subject to donor's tax under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practical terms, since the donation of ₱200,000 does not exceed the annual exclusion limit of ₱250,000, it is not subject to donor's tax. Therefore, the donor does not need to file a donor's tax return or pay any tax on this amount. However, it is essential to keep records of the donation for future reference, especially if additional gifts are made within the same year that could cumulatively exceed the threshold.",
